WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.343
A useful alert tells the right reviewer about an event that may require a defined action.

00:00:07.343 --> 00:00:18.044
It should include camera, time, zone, event type, representative image or clip, model version, confidence signal, and enough preceding and following context for confirmation.

00:00:18.044 --> 00:00:21.611
Thresholds should reflect consequence and local conditions.

00:00:21.611 --> 00:00:26.856
A lower threshold may catch more events while increasing false positives.

00:00:26.856 --> 00:00:35.458
Schedules, regions of interest, direction, duration, and object size can make alerts more relevant without pretending uncertainty is gone.

00:00:35.458 --> 00:00:39.865
Group repeated frames and related detections into one event.

00:00:39.865 --> 00:00:46.788
Cooldown periods and escalation rules prevent a single ongoing condition from generating dozens of notifications.

00:00:46.788 --> 00:00:54.551
Route routine review to a queue and reserve immediate alerts for cases with a clear, time-sensitive response.

00:00:54.551 --> 00:00:58.118
Human review is essential before meaningful action.

00:00:58.118 --> 00:01:03.783
Reviewers should be able to confirm, dismiss, defer, add context, and escalate.

00:01:03.783 --> 00:01:12.386
When confidence is low or footage is unclear, the system should communicate uncertainty rather than automatically assume the worst.

00:01:12.386 --> 00:01:15.113
Document review decisions and outcomes.

00:01:15.113 --> 00:01:22.037
Feedback reveals confusing camera angles, recurring harmless activity, model drift, and rules that need tuning.

00:01:22.037 --> 00:01:27.702
Access to review queues and footage should follow role and privacy policy.

00:01:27.702 --> 00:01:35.465
Measure alert quality through confirmed relevance, missed events, review time, duplicate rate, escalation outcome, and reviewer feedback.

00:01:35.465 --> 00:01:44.487
Alerting is successful when it supports timely, accountable judgment without overwhelming people or turning uncertain model output into automatic accusation.
